      {
        "id": "section_1",
        "narration": "You've typed a function parameter as `any` just to get your code compiling, haven't you? We've all done it. But the second you use `any`, you strip away every single safety guarantee TypeScript gives you. You lose autocomplete, you lose compile-time checking, and you invite runtime crashes into production. <break time='0.6s'/> Generics exist to solve this exact dilemma: they give you ultimate flexibility without throwing away type safety.",
        "objective": "",
        "visuals": [
