      {
        "id": "section_4",
        "narration": "Generics aren't just academic syntax or visual clutter in your codebase. They're the core engine that powers type inference across every major library you use — from React hooks to Zod schemas. <break time='0.6s'/> Next time you feel tempted to type a parameter as `any` or write five duplicate functions, write a single generic signature instead. Your editor will thank you, and your production logs will stay clean.",
        "objective": "",
